@* The application's build identity, centred at the foot of every page: the release, the environment, the
   commit and the pipeline run, so a viewer can say which artifact is on screen. All four are stamped into
   the artifact this page was served from, and the same four ride every metric in Application Insights.

   None of the four designs draws a footer, so this is a deliberate addition to them, recorded here
   rather than silently. Its styling is the header's instead of a new vocabulary - the same
   --surface, --on-surface-variant and label-sm - so the two ends of a page read as a pair, and it
   carries no separator: the footer is the page's own end rather than a band across it.

   It is the same on every page, including the builder, where the selection panel stops above it
   rather than sitting over it. Nothing here has to know which page it is on. *@
<footer class="app-footer" aria-label="Build">
    <div class="container app-footer__inner">
        <span class="app-footer__build">@AppBuildIdentity.Current.Label</span>
    </div>
</footer>
